cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper."
type: software
title: "A readout floor can hide a secular growth of the energy error from an absolute-level diagnostic"
abstract: "Code and data accompanying the paper 'A readout floor can hide a secular growth of the energy error from an absolute-level diagnostic'. It contains the experiment scripts that produce every measured number in the paper, the committed JSON and NPZ outputs of those scripts, the four figure scripts, the trained defect-corrector checkpoints and a single-command reproduction driver (repro.py). The physical setting is a charged particle in a nonstationary magnetic field integrated by the Boris scheme, by a learned defect corrector with a hard speed-constraint projection, and by five classical schemes for comparison; the analysis separates the magnitude and direction channels of the velocity error, measures the readout floor of the energy error, and tests the growth-exponent law and the four-probe validation protocol of the paper."
